{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TLzzG691gX7pFYk9HjRdMu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Claims require softening but paper remains viable. C1 holds but\n2\t  generalization downgrades from \"across judges and benchmarks\" to \"demonstrated on\n3\t  GPT-4o, replicated on Gemini-Flash, with supporting evidence on AlpacaEval.\" C2\n4\t  remains headline but qualified: \"Likert Blindspot is robust for strong-bias conditions\n5\t  (GPT-4o × formality on LLMBar) but gap magnitude is condition-dependent; at n=500\n6\t  binarized Likert approaches significance → Blindspot is primarily an efficiency\n7\t  gap (~2× Cohen''s h), not absolute insensitivity.\" C3 drops \"multi-axis\" — formality\n8\t  is validated, verbosity is \"suggestive\" (H1 PASS but scoring blocked), tone/register\n9\t  are method boundaries. C4 provides detection guidance only; no correction formula\n10\t  without multi-cell backing. RATE differentiation paragraph works (RATE uses Likert\n11\t  ATE → our C2 applies to RATE itself) but is speculative without RATE replication\n12\t  data. Direction asymmetry varies by judge → no unified causal narrative across judges.\n13\t  Compensate with deeper methodological analysis (why does GPT-4o × LLMBar work so\n14\t  well?), honest boundary characterization, power analysis as practical tool, stronger\n15\t  psychometric lineage framing. Target: EMNLP 2026 Findings (confident) / Main (borderline,\n16\t  needs strong rebuttal on generalization). Expected ARR score: 3.0–3.5.\n17\t\n18\t  '\n19\timagined_experiments:\n20\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n21\t  plan_id: exp-001\n22\t  description: '在 Claude-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 LLMBar formality pairwise 实验。\n23\t    使用已有 counterfactuals，200 pairwise calls × 2 directions per judge， position-controlled\n24\t    dual-direction protocol。\n25\t\n26\t    '\n27\t  expected_results:\n28\t    claude_sonnet:\n29\t      n_valid_both_trials: 96\n30\t      n_consistent: 50\n31\t      consistency_rate: 0.521\n32\t      formal_wins: 29\n33\t      casual_wins: 21\n34\t      formal_win_rate: 0.58\n35\t      wilson_ci:\n36\t      - 0.442\n37\t      - 0.706\n38\t      sign_test_p: 0.161\n39\t      position_bias_overall_A: 0.52\n40\t      direction_formal_to_casual:\n41\t        n: 30\n42\t        formal_wins: 19\n43\t        win_rate: 0.633\n44\t        p: 0.1\n45\t      direction_casual_to_formal:\n46\t        n: 20\n47\t        formal_wins: 10\n48\t        win_rate: 0.5\n49\t        p: 1.0\n50\t    gemini_20_flash:\n51\t      n_valid_both_trials: 97\n52\t      n_consistent: 47\n53\t      consistency_rate: 0.485\n54\t      formal_wins: 30\n55\t      casual_wins: 17\n56\t      formal_win_rate: 0.638\n57\t      wilson_ci:\n58\t      - 0.495\n59\t      - 0.761\n60\t      sign_test_p: 0.041\n61\t      position_bias_overall_A: 0.56\n62\t      direction_formal_to_casual:\n63\t        n: 28\n64\t        formal_wins: 22\n65\t        win_rate: 0.786\n66\t        p: 0.002\n67\t      direction_casual_to_formal:\n68\t        n: 19\n69\t        formal_wins: 8\n70\t        win_rate: 0.421\n71\t        p: 0.648\n72\t    cross_judge_summary:\n73\t      judges_significant_p005: 1\n74\t      judges_marginal_p005_015: 1\n75\t      judges_null: 0\n76\t      gpt4o_reference_win_rate: 0.691\n77\t      best_non_gpt4o_win_rate: 0.638\n78\t      win_rate_attenuation_vs_gpt4o: 0.053\n79\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档预测 style bias 是真实效应但跨 judge 有系统性衰减。Gemini-Flash 显著 (p=0.041)\n80\t    的机制：Flash 模型的 RLHF 投入较少 debiasing → 保留更强的 surface style preference；但效应量从 GPT-4o\n81\t    的 69.1% 衰减到 63.8%，因为 Gemini 的 pairwise 一致性率较低 (48.5% vs GPT-4o 56.1%)，引入更多噪声对。Claude-Sonnet\n82\t    不显著 (p=0.161) 的机制：Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程更保守，Constitutional AI 训练 可能部分抑制 surface style\n83\t    preference；加上 Claude 的 consistency_rate 只有 52.1%，有效 n 从 50 对中仅 29 个 formal wins\n84\t    → 检验力不足。Direction asymmetry 的 judge 间差异是 median 档的关键特征：Gemini 与 GPT-4o 类似，formal→casual\n85\t    方向强 (78.6%)、casual→formal 方向 null (42.1%)；但 Claude 的不对称性更弱 (63.3% vs 50.0%)，且\n86\t    casual→formal 方向完全平坦。这使得 \"formal→casual 方向 驱动效应\" 的叙事不能跨 judge 推广——只能说 \"direction\n87\t    asymmetry is judge-dependent, consistently observed for GPT-4o and Gemini but\n88\t    not Claude.\" 一致性率的 judge 间差异本身值得报告：它反映不同 judge 的 position sensitivity， 不是方法的失败而是\n89\t    judge 特性的测量。\n90\t\n91\t    '\n92\t  tables:\n93\t  - name: 'Table 2a: Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar)'\n94\t    description: '3 rows (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) × columns: n_consistent,\n95\t      consistency_rate, formal_win_rate, 95% Wilson CI, sign_test_p, formal→casual_win_rate,\n96\t      casual→formal_win_rate, position_bias. GPT-4o 行 bolded (primary)，Gemini 行 starred\n97\t      (significant replication)。\n98\t\n99\t      '\n100\t  figures_description:\n101\t  - 'Forest plot: formal_win_rate with 95% Wilson CI for 3 judges。Vertical dashed\n102\t    line at 50%。GPT-4o CI clearly right of 50%；Gemini CI right but wider，lower bound\n103\t    near 50%；Claude CI straddling 50%。Annotate p-values next to each bar。\n104\t\n105\t    '\n106\t  analysis: 'C1 表述降级为 \"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006), replicated on Gemini-Flash\n107\t    (p=0.041), not detected on Claude-Sonnet (p=0.161, possibly underpowered).\" Claude\n108\t    的 null 不能确定是 \"无 bias\" 还是 \"power 不足\"——需在论文中讨论 power (at n=50 consistent, MDE≈0.18\n109\t    for pairwise win_rate → 58% 在 detection boundary 上)。Direction asymmetry 的 judge\n110\t    间差异增加了 §5 Discussion 的复杂度但也增加 了 depth——\"why does asymmetry vary?\" 可以链接到 judge\n111\t    的 RLHF 训练差异。\n112\t\n113\t    '\n114\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n115\t  plan_id: exp-002\n116\t  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上新生成 formality counterfactuals，GPT-4o + Claude-Sonnet\n117\t    + Gemini-Flash 作为 judge 运行完整 CSD pairwise pipeline。\n118\t\n119\t    '\n120\t  expected_results:\n121\t    counterfactual_generation:\n122\t      alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n123\t      alpacaeval_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.79\n124\t      alpacaeval_both_pass_rate: 0.78\n125\t      mtbench_nli_pass_rate: 0.79\n126\t      mtbench_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.74\n127\t      mtbench_both_pass_rate: 0.72\n128\t      note: NLI pass rate drops vs LLMBar (0.88) due to more diverse/technical source\n129\t        texts\n130\t    alpacaeval:\n131\t      gpt4o:\n132\t        n_consistent: 51\n133\t        formal_win_rate: 0.608\n134\t        sign_test_p: 0.072\n135\t        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.7\n136\t        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n137\t      claude_sonnet:\n138\t        n_consistent: 44\n139\t        formal_win_rate: 0.545\n140\t        sign_test_p: 0.348\n141\t        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.58\n142\t        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n143\t      gemini_flash:\n144\t        n_consistent: 42\n145\t        formal_win_rate: 0.595\n146\t        sign_test_p: 0.109\n147\t        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.68\n148\t        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.48\n149\t    mt_bench:\n150\t      gpt4o:\n151\t        n_consistent: 46\n152\t        formal_win_rate: 0.565\n153\t        sign_test_p: 0.214\n154\t        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.62\n155\t        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n156\t      claude_sonnet:\n157\t        n_consistent: 40\n158\t        formal_win_rate: 0.525\n159\t        sign_test_p: 0.557\n160\t        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.54\n161\t        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n162\t      gemini_flash:\n163\t        n_consistent: 39\n164\t        formal_win_rate: 0.538\n165\t        sign_test_p: 0.396\n166\t        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.6\n167\t        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.47\n168\t    cross_benchmark_summary:\n169\t      cells_significant_p005: 0\n170\t      cells_trend_p005_010: 1\n171\t      cells_trend_p010_015: 1\n172\t      cells_null: 4\n173\t      benchmark_ordering: LLMBar >> AlpacaEval > MT-Bench\n174\t      nli_pass_rate_ordering: LLMBar (0.88) > AlpacaEval (0.83) > MT-Bench (0.79)\n175\t  result_rationale: '新 benchmark 效应衰减是 median 档的核心预测。两个独立机制叠加造成衰减： (1) Counterfactual\n176\t    质量下降——LLMBar 源文本是简洁的 instruction-following 对， formality rewriting 容易保内容；AlpacaEval\n177\t    文本更长更多样，NLI pass rate 从 0.88 降到 0.83，丢弃更多样本 → 有效 n 减少；MT-Bench 包含数学/代码/推理等 domain\n178\t    特异性强的文本，formality rewriting 更容易改变内容（把 \"Let''s solve this step by step\" 改成正式版本可能改变推理链结构）→\n179\t    NLI 降到 0.79。 (2) Formality 方差差异——LLMBar 的 instruction-following 文本天然有较大的 formality\n180\t    方差（有的回答很 casual，有的很 formal），counterfactual contrast 大； MT-Bench 的技术性文本天然偏 formal，formality\n181\t    rewriting 的 contrast 小 → smaller effect size。GPT-4o × AlpacaEval 的 p=0.072 (trend)\n182\t    符合 median 核心 假设 \"1 additional benchmark shows trend (p<0.10) but not clean significance\"。\n183\t    Holm-Bonferroni 校正 (within GPT-4o: 0.006, 0.072, 0.214 → adjusted 0.018, 0.144,\n184\t    0.214) 后只有 LLMBar survive。论文需诚实报告：\"effect replicates as trend on AlpacaEval but\n185\t    not MT-Bench\" 并讨论 benchmark 依赖性原因。\n186\t\n187\t    '\n188\t  tables:\n189\t  - name: 'Table 2b: Full 3×3 judge × benchmark pairwise results'\n190\t    description: '9-cell grid。Rows: LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench。Columns grouped by\n191\t      judge， each showing formal_win_rate (p-value)。p<0.05 bolded，p<0.10 italicized。\n192\t      Only 2 bold cells (GPT-4o×LLMBar, Gemini×LLMBar)，2 italic (GPT-4o×AlpacaEval,\n193\t      Gemini×AlpacaEval)。Additional column: NLI pass rate per benchmark。\n194\t\n195\t      '\n196\t  figures_description:\n197\t  - 'Heatmap: 3×3 grid，color = formal_win_rate (diverging colormap centered at 50%)。\n198\t    Cell annotations: win_rate% (p=x.xx)。Clear gradient: LLMBar row warmest， MT-Bench\n199\t    row coolest。Column gradient: GPT-4o warmest，Claude coolest。\n200\t\n201\t    '\n202\t  analysis: 'exp-002 确认 formality bias 不是 LLMBar artifact——AlpacaEval 上 GPT-4o 和 Gemini\n203\t    都显示 trend (p<0.12)——但 effect magnitude 确实 benchmark-dependent。 论文需要 §5.1 \"Benchmark\n204\t    Dependence\" 讨论三个 benchmark 的差异，linking to counterfactual quality (NLI pass rate)\n205\t    和 formality 方差。MT-Bench 的 null 结果 本身有 method boundary 意义：when source texts are\n206\t    domain-specific/technical， formality rewriting 更可能失败 NLI gate → CSD 方法自动 degrades\n207\t    gracefully。 Claim 从 \"across benchmarks\" 降级为 \"demonstrated on LLMBar, supporting\n208\t    trend on AlpacaEval (instruction-following), inconclusive on MT-Bench (task-specific).\"\n209\t\n210\t    '\n211\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n212\t  plan_id: exp-003\n213\t  description: '对 9 个 judge × benchmark cells 系统计算 Likert ATE 和 binarized Likert sign\n214\t    test，与 pairwise win rate 对比。量化 C2 Likert Blindspot 的 replication rate 和 condition-dependence。\n215\t\n216\t    '\n217\t  expected_results:\n218\t    likert_ate:\n219\t      gpt4o_llmbar:\n220\t        ate: -0.102\n221\t        se: 0.149\n222\t        p: 0.332\n223\t      gpt4o_alpacaeval:\n224\t        ate: -0.07\n225\t        se: 0.155\n226\t        p: 0.48\n227\t      gpt4o_mtbench:\n228\t        ate: -0.04\n229\t        se: 0.161\n230\t        p: 0.69\n231\t      claude_llmbar:\n232\t        ate: 0.03\n233\t        se: 0.158\n234\t        p: 0.71\n235\t      claude_alpacaeval:\n236\t        ate: -0.01\n237\t        se: 0.165\n238\t        p: 0.88\n239\t      claude_mtbench:\n240\t        ate: 0.02\n241\t        se: 0.17\n242\t        p: 0.82\n243\t      gemini_llmbar:\n244\t        ate: -0.09\n245\t        se: 0.152\n246\t        p: 0.39\n247\t      gemini_alpacaeval:\n248\t        ate: -0.06\n249\t        se: 0.16\n250\t        p: 0.53\n251\t      gemini_mtbench:\n252\t        ate: -0.03\n253\t        se: 0.168\n254\t        p: 0.76\n255\t      any_significant: false\n256\t      note: Likert ATE non-significant in all 9 cells; continuous Likert uniformly\n257\t        insensitive\n258\t    binarized_likert:\n259\t      gpt4o_llmbar:\n260\t        n_nontie: 33\n261\t        win_rate: 0.606\n262\t        p: 0.296\n263\t        status: non-significant\n264\t      gpt4o_alpacaeval:\n265\t        n_nontie: 29\n266\t        win_rate: 0.586\n267\t        p: 0.108\n268\t        status: ambiguous\n269\t      gpt4o_mtbench:\n270\t        n_nontie: 26\n271\t        win_rate: 0.538\n272\t        p: 0.422\n273\t        status: non-significant\n274\t      claude_llmbar:\n275\t        n_nontie: 27\n276\t        win_rate: 0.556\n277\t        p: 0.248\n278\t        status: non-significant\n279\t      claude_alpacaeval:\n280\t        n_nontie: 23\n281\t        win_rate: 0.522\n282\t        p: 0.621\n283\t        status: non-significant\n284\t      claude_mtbench:\n285\t        n_nontie: 21\n286\t        win_rate: 0.524\n287\t        p: 0.617\n288\t        status: non-significant\n289\t      gemini_llmbar:\n290\t        n_nontie: 30\n291\t        win_rate: 0.6\n292\t        p: 0.098\n293\t        status: ambiguous\n294\t      gemini_alpacaeval:\n295\t        n_nontie: 25\n296\t        win_rate: 0.56\n297\t        p: 0.23\n298\t        status: non-significant\n299\t      gemini_mtbench:\n300\t        n_nontie: 22\n301\t        win_rate: 0.5\n302\t        p: 1.0\n303\t        status: non-significant\n304\t    binarized_likert_summary:\n305\t      non_significant_cells: 7\n306\t      ambiguous_cells_p005_012: 2\n307\t      significant_cells: 0\n308\t    c2_gap_analysis:\n309\t      cells_pairwise_sig_AND_likert_not: 2\n310\t      cells_pairwise_sig_AND_binarized_ambiguous: 1\n311\t      cells_pairwise_trend_AND_binarized_ambiguous: 1\n312\t      cells_both_non_sig: 5\n313\t      c2_clean_replication_rate: 0.67\n314\t      c2_with_ambiguous: 0.5\n315\t    measurement_amplification:\n316\t      mean_pairwise_effect_over_50pct: 0.074\n317\t      mean_binarized_likert_effect_over_50pct: 0.044\n318\t      amplification_ratio: 1.68\n319\t  result_rationale: 'Likert ATE 全面不显著是 median 档的稳健预测——continuous Likert 的 within-pair\n320\t    评分方差 (SE~0.15-0.17) 远大于 formality ATE (~0.05-0.10)，信噪比根本不足。 这是 structural 而非 power\n321\t    issue：即使 n→∞，如果 ATE 接近零（raw ATE 在 -0.10 到 +0.03 之间散布），continuous Likert 的 measurement\n322\t    noise 使得 effect 不 convergent。Binarized Likert 的 2 个 ambiguous cells 是 C2 的最大叙事张力：\n323\t    (a) Gemini×LLMBar binarized p=0.098 vs pairwise p=0.041——gap 存在但不大， reviewer 会质疑\n324\t    \"is this just a power issue?\" 回答：effect size 差异（63.8% vs 60.0%）说明 pairwise 不仅\n325\t    more powerful 而且 amplifies the signal—— amplification ratio 1.68× 是 structural\n326\t    advantage（pairwise 的 forced choice 消除了 Likert 的 tie/neutral responses 噪声）。(b)\n327\t    GPT-4o×AlpacaEval binarized p=0.108 vs pairwise p=0.072——两个都 marginal，gap 极小 →\n328\t    这个 cell 不支持 C2。但在 5 个 null cells 中，pairwise 和 binarized Likert 都 null → C2 gap\n329\t    只在 effect 存在时才有意义。整体：C2 replication rate 67%（2/3 significant pairwise cells 有\n330\t    clean gap），但加入 ambiguous 考量降到 50%。论文需要 nuanced 表述：\"The Likert Blindspot is most\n331\t    pronounced when style bias is moderate (pairwise 60-70%); for strong effects,\n332\t    binarized Likert may approach detection; for null effects, no method detects.\"\n333\t\n334\t    '\n335\t  tables:\n336\t  - name: 'Table 3: Main results — Pairwise vs Likert vs Binarized Likert (9 cells)'\n337\t    description: 'Paper 的 main result table。9-cell grid (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)，\n338\t      each cell: Pairwise win_rate (p) | Likert ATE (p) | Binarized win_rate (p)。\n339\t      Color coding: green p<0.05, yellow p<0.12, red p>0.12。 Final row: measurement\n340\t      amplification ratio per cell。\n341\t\n342\t      '\n343\t  - name: 'Table S1: C2 gap categorization'\n344\t    description: 'Supplementary。Rows: 9 cells。Columns: pairwise_status (sig/marginal/null),\n345\t      binarized_status (non-sig/ambiguous), C2_gap (clean/ambiguous/no gap/NA)。 Summary:\n346\t      2 clean, 1 ambiguous, 1 marginal-both, 5 both-null。\n347\t\n348\t      '\n349\t  figures_description:\n350\t  - 'Paired lollipop chart: 9 cells on y-axis，for each cell two dots connected by\n351\t    line — pairwise win_rate (blue) and binarized Likert win_rate (orange)。 Vertical\n352\t    dashed at 50%。Gap between dots = C2 blindspot magnitude per cell。 Cells ordered\n353\t    by pairwise effect size。Clearly shows pairwise dots consistently further from\n354\t    50% than binarized Likert dots。\n355\t\n356\t    '\n357\t  - 'Scatter: x = pairwise win_rate, y = binarized Likert win_rate, one point per\n358\t    cell。 y=x diagonal line。All points below diagonal → pairwise always ≥ binarized。\n359\t    Regression line slope < 1 → amplification ratio quantified。\n360\t\n361\t    '\n362\t  analysis: 'exp-003 是论文最重要的表格。Median 结果的叙事策略：(1) Lead with Likert ATE = 0/9 significant\n363\t    → continuous Likert 完全 blind，这是最强 version of C2；(2) Binarized Likert = 0/9 significant\n364\t    (2 ambiguous) vs Pairwise = 2/9 significant → gap exists but C2 需要 qualify 为 \"Likert\n365\t    Blindspot is a measurement efficiency gap, not absolute insensitivity\"；(3) Amplification\n366\t    ratio 1.68× provides quantitative hook for practitioners。§5.2 \"When Does the Blindspot\n367\t    Narrow?\" 分析 C2 gap 与 effect size 的关系——如果 pairwise effect 越大 gap 越大 (positive correlation)，说明\n368\t    Likert 对所有 effect size 都 equally insensitive (stronger C2)；如果 gap 恒定， 说明只是 constant\n369\t    offset (weaker C2 but still useful)。\n370\t\n371\t    '\n372\t- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n373\t  plan_id: exp-005\n374\t  description: '对所有 judge × benchmark 组合做 original vs double-rewrite pairwise comparison，\n375\t    量化 original preference confound。扩展 exp-014 的 GEE logistic decomposition 到所有条件。\n376\t\n377\t    '\n378\t  expected_results:\n379\t    original_preference_pairwise:\n380\t      gpt4o_llmbar:\n381\t        original_pref_win_rate: 0.585\n382\t        original_pref_p: 0.052\n383\t        gee_original_OR: 1.82\n384\t        gee_original_p: 0.052\n385\t        note: known from exp-014\n386\t      claude_llmbar:\n387\t        original_pref_win_rate: 0.545\n388\t        original_pref_p: 0.232\n389\t        gee_original_OR: 1.38\n390\t        gee_original_p: 0.245\n391\t      gemini_llmbar:\n392\t        original_pref_win_rate: 0.625\n393\t        original_pref_p: 0.026\n394\t        gee_original_OR: 2.18\n395\t        gee_original_p: 0.03\n396\t      gpt4o_alpacaeval:\n397\t        original_pref_win_rate: 0.57\n398\t        original_pref_p: 0.105\n399\t        gee_original_OR: 1.58\n400\t        gee_original_p: 0.112\n401\t      claude_alpacaeval:\n402\t        original_pref_win_rate: 0.53\n403\t        original_pref_p: 0.396\n404\t        gee_original_OR: 1.22\n405\t        gee_original_p: 0.41\n406\t      gemini_alpacaeval:\n407\t        original_pref_win_rate: 0.58\n408\t        original_pref_p: 0.075\n409\t        gee_original_OR: 1.72\n410\t        gee_original_p: 0.082\n411\t    logistic_decomposition_extended:\n412\t      gpt4o_llmbar:\n413\t        formality_OR: 2.21\n414\t        formality_p: 0.01\n415\t        original_OR: 1.82\n416\t        original_p: 0.052\n417\t        formality_exceeds_original: true\n418\t      gemini_llmbar:\n419\t        formality_OR: 1.95\n420\t        formality_p: 0.038\n421\t        original_OR: 2.18\n422\t        original_p: 0.03\n423\t        formality_exceeds_original: false\n424\t        note: 'CRITICAL: original preference OR exceeds formality OR for Gemini'\n425\t      claude_llmbar:\n426\t        formality_OR: 1.52\n427\t        formality_p: 0.165\n428\t        original_OR: 1.38\n429\t        original_p: 0.245\n430\t        formality_exceeds_original: true\n431\t        note: neither significant — underpowered\n432\t    summary:\n433\t      judges_with_significant_original_pref: 1\n434\t      judges_with_marginal_original_pref: 2\n435\t      formality_still_dominates_for_gpt4o: true\n436\t      confound_problematic_for_gemini: true\n437\t  result_rationale: 'Original preference confound 在 median 档变得 judge-dependent，核心威胁来自\n438\t    Gemini。机制：double-rewrite 虽设计为 style-preserving，仍不可避免引入 surface 变化（lexical micro-substitutions,\n439\t    sentence structure 微调）。不同 judge 对 这些 \"rewriting artifacts\" 的敏感度不同。Gemini-Flash\n440\t    作为较小模型，对 surface form 变化更敏感 → double-rewrite 产生的微小质量损失被 Gemini 放大为显著 original\n441\t    preference (OR=2.18, p=0.026)。关键问题：Gemini×LLMBar 的 formality pairwise 显著 (p=0.041)，但\n442\t    original preference 也显著 (p=0.026)，且 original OR (2.18) > formality OR (1.95) →\n443\t    对 Gemini 来说，无法 cleanly separate formality bias from rewriting artifact。GPT-4o×LLMBar\n444\t    保持 clean：formality OR (2.21) > original OR (1.82)，formality p=0.010 vs original\n445\t    p=0.052 → 可以 argue formality is the dominant effect。Claude 两者都不显著，无信息量。论文策略： primary\n446\t    claim 基于 GPT-4o×LLMBar (clean decomposition)；Gemini 的显著结果作为 \"replication with\n447\t    caveat\" — \"formality bias detected (p=0.041) but original preference cannot be\n448\t    ruled out as partial contributor (p=0.026).\" 这种 honesty 是 strength not weakness\n449\t    — reviewer 更信任 acknowledged confounds。\n450\t\n451\t    '\n452\t  tables:\n453\t  - name: 'Table 4: Original preference decomposition across judges'\n454\t    description: 'Rows: judge × benchmark (6 cells with data)。Columns: formality_OR\n455\t      (CI, p), original_pref_OR (CI, p), formality > original?, status。 GPT-4o×LLMBar\n456\t      highlighted as clean decomposition；Gemini×LLMBar flagged。\n457\t\n458\t      '\n459\t  figures_description:\n460\t  - 'Paired forest plot: for each cell，two horizontal bars with 95% CI — formality\n461\t    OR (blue) and original preference OR (red)。Vertical line at OR=1。 GPT-4o×LLMBar:\n462\t    blue clearly right, red CI crossing 1。 Gemini×LLMBar: both right of 1 with overlapping\n463\t    CIs → confound visible。\n464\t\n465\t    '\n466\t  analysis: 'exp-005 使得 \"confound is negligible\" argument 不成立。但 \"confound is acknowledged\n467\t    and statistically controlled\" 在 GPT-4o 上仍然成立。对于 Gemini， 论文需要 paragraph: \"Gemini-Flash\n468\t    shows both formality preference and original preference; future work with larger\n469\t    n or improved double-rewrite protocol may achieve cleaner separation.\" 这实际上提供了有用的\n470\t    method boundary：CSD 的 confound control 对某些 judge 更 effective（GPT-4o）比其他（Gemini）。\n471\t    Practical implication for C4：recommend running original-preference control for\n472\t    each judge, and only report formality estimates where decomposition is clean。\n473\t\n474\t    '\n475\t- name: Scaled replication (n=500)\n476\t  plan_id: exp-006\n477\t  description: 'GPT-4o × LLMBar (最佳 cell) 从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。计算 pairwise、 binarized\n478\t    Likert、Likert ATE，直接检验 C2 是 structural blindspot 还是 power issue。Power analysis\n479\t    量化 measurement efficiency gap。\n480\t\n481\t    '\n482\t  expected_results:\n483\t    pairwise:\n484\t      n_total: 500\n485\t      n_valid_both_trials: 490\n486\t      n_consistent: 275\n487\t      consistency_rate: 0.561\n488\t      formal_wins: 168\n489\t      casual_wins: 107\n490\t      formal_win_rate: 0.611\n491\t      wilson_ci:\n492\t      - 0.552\n493\t      - 0.667\n494\t      sign_test_p: 0.0004\n495\t    binarized_likert:\n496\t      n_nli_ge90: 435\n497\t      n_nontie: 163\n498\t      formal_direction: 94\n499\t      formal_win_rate: 0.577\n500\t      sign_test_p: 0.063\n501\t      wilson_ci:\n502\t      - 0.499\n503\t      - 0.651\n504\t      note: Approaches significance; NOT significant at alpha=0.05\n505\t    likert_ate:\n506\t      n_primary: 435\n507\t      raw_ate: -0.085\n508\t      raw_se: 0.065\n509\t      raw_p: 0.19\n510\t      corrected_ate: 0.095\n511\t      corrected_se: 0.047\n512\t      corrected_p: 0.043\n513\t      note: Raw ATE still wrong direction; corrected ATE barely significant\n514\t    power_analysis:\n515\t      pairwise_detected_effect_cohens_h: 0.222\n516\t      binarized_likert_detected_effect_cohens_h: 0.154\n517\t      measurement_amplification_ratio: 1.44\n518\t      pairwise_power_at_n100: 0.72\n519\t      pairwise_power_at_n200: 0.93\n520\t      pairwise_power_at_n500: 0.998\n521\t      binarized_likert_power_at_n100: 0.18\n522\t      binarized_likert_power_at_n200: 0.34\n523\t      binarized_likert_power_at_n500: 0.52\n524\t      binarized_likert_n_for_80pct_power: 680\n525\t      likert_ate_power_at_n100: 0.09\n526\t      likert_ate_power_at_n500: 0.31\n527\t      likert_ate_n_for_80pct_power: 1200\n528\t    regression_to_mean:\n529\t      n100_pairwise_win_rate: 0.691\n530\t      n500_pairwise_win_rate: 0.611\n531\t      regression_magnitude: 0.08\n532\t      note: 8pp regression consistent with sampling variance at n=55 consistent pairs\n533\t  result_rationale: 'n=500 的三个关键结果及其 rationale： (1) Pairwise win rate 从 69.1% 回归到\n534\t    61.1%。n=100 的 69.1% 来自仅 55 个 consistent pairs → 采样方差大，Wilson CI [56.0%, 79.7%]。n=500\n535\t    的 275 个 consistent pairs 给出更精确的 true effect estimate ~61%。8pp 回归幅度在 n=55 的 CI\n536\t    范围内，统计上完全预期。效应仍高度显著 (p=0.0004)。 (2) Binarized Likert p=0.063：在 n=500 下 approaching\n537\t    但 NOT crossing 0.05 线。 这是 median 档的精妙预测——如果 binarized Likert 真的 significant，C2\n538\t    从 \"blindspot\" 变成 \"efficiency gap\"，论文核心受损；如果完全 null，C2 过于强势 反而可疑。p=0.063 恰好在模糊地带：它说明\n539\t    binarized Likert 不是完全 blind（有 trending signal），但需要远超 pairwise 的样本量才能 detect →\n540\t    \"efficiency gap\" framing 是准确的。关键：binarized Likert n_nontie=163 (Likert 评分相同的 pair\n541\t    被丢弃 → 信息损失)，effective n 仅 pairwise 的 59%，这是 structural 不是 power。 (3) Likert ATE\n542\t    raw p=0.19 仍不显著且方向错误 → continuous Likert 在 n=500 下 仍然 blind。Corrected ATE (accounting\n543\t    for rewrite bias) p=0.043 barely significant，但 \"corrected\" 需要知道 rewrite bias →\n544\t    不是 post-hoc 可用的检测 工具。这进一步支持 \"Likert cannot serve as style bias detector without\n545\t    correction.\" Power analysis 的实用价值：pairwise 在 n=100 就有 72% power (接近 80%)， binarized\n546\t    Likert 需要 n=680 for 80% power → 6.8× 样本量差距。这是论文的 quantitative C2 claim：\"pairwise\n547\t    comparison is ~7× more sample-efficient than binarized Likert for detecting style\n548\t    bias at the observed effect size.\"\n549\t\n550\t    '\n551\t  tables:\n552\t  - name: 'Table 5: Scaled replication — measurement comparison at n=500'\n553\t    description: '3 rows (Pairwise, Binarized Likert, Likert ATE) × columns: n_effective,\n554\t      effect_estimate, 95% CI, p-value, Cohen''s h, power_at_n100, power_at_n500,\n555\t      n_for_80pct_power。Clearly shows efficiency hierarchy。\n556\t\n557\t      '\n558\t  - name: 'Table S2: n=100 vs n=500 comparison'\n559\t    description: 'Side-by-side: all metrics at two sample sizes。Regression to mean\n560\t      quantified and contextualized。\n561\t\n562\t      '\n563\t  figures_description:\n564\t  - 'Power curve: x = total sample size (50 to 1000), y = statistical power (0 to\n565\t    1)。 Three curves: pairwise (blue, crosses 80% at ~110), binarized Likert (orange,\n566\t    crosses 80% at ~680), Likert ATE (red, crosses 80% at ~1200)。Horizontal dashed\n567\t    at 80%。Vertical dashed at n=100 and n=500。This is C2''s key visualization — the\n568\t    efficiency gap is immediately visible。\n569\t\n570\t    '\n571\t  - 'Running estimate plot: x = cumulative n (in increments of 50), y = pairwise win_rate\n572\t    with running 95% CI ribbon。Shows convergence from volatile ~69% at n=100 toward\n573\t    stable ~61% at n=500。Communicates regression to mean visually。\n574\t\n575\t    '\n576\t  analysis: 'exp-006 redefines C2 from \"Likert Blindspot\" to \"Likert Efficiency Gap.\"\n577\t    Binarized Likert p=0.063 at n=500 means the effect is detectable in principle\n578\t    — given enough data. But the practical gap (pairwise needs n~110, binarized Likert\n579\t    needs n~680) is the real contribution. For practitioners: \"If you suspect style\n580\t    bias, pairwise comparison with n=100 is sufficient; Likert scoring would need\n581\t    n≥700 for the same statistical power.\" Title 可能需要从 \"Blindspot\" 软化为 \"Blind Spot\"\n582\t    或保留但 在 abstract 中 qualify。Power analysis table 是最 reviewer-friendly 的结果之一—— 直接\n583\t    actionable guidance。Win rate 回归到 61.1% 需要 honestly report，不要 buried in supplement。\n584\t\n585\t    '\n586\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n587\t  plan_id: exp-009\n588\t  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上 重复 formality\n589\t    counterfactual generation + pairwise pipeline。排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n590\t\n591\t    '\n592\t  expected_results:\n593\t    counterfactual_quality:\n594\t      nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n595\t      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.75\n596\t      both_pass_rate: 0.73\n597\t      nli_mean: 0.869\n598\t      bertscore_mean: 0.905\n599\t      nli_std: 0.298\n600\t      comparison_vs_qwen:\n601\t        qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n602\t        qwen_both_pass_rate: 0.88\n603\t        llama_nli_delta: -0.07\n604\t        note: Llama slightly worse at style transfer precision\n605\t    pairwise_results:\n606\t      n_valid_both_trials: 95\n607\t      n_consistent: 48\n608\t      consistency_rate: 0.505\n609\t      formal_wins: 30\n610\t      casual_wins: 18\n611\t      formal_win_rate: 0.625\n612\t      wilson_ci:\n613\t      - 0.48\n614\t      - 0.749\n615\t      sign_test_p: 0.042\n616\t      direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.72\n617\t      direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n618\t    comparison_with_qwen:\n619\t      qwen_win_rate: 0.691\n620\t      llama_win_rate: 0.625\n621\t      difference: 0.066\n622\t      difference_p: 0.43\n623\t      direction_consistent: true\n624\t      sign_consistent: true\n625\t      magnitude_within_qwen_ci: true\n626\t      note: 6.6pp difference not significant; both within Qwen's [56.0%, 79.7%] CI\n627\t  result_rationale: 'Llama-3.1-70B 的 style transfer 质量略低于 Qwen3-32B 是预期中的——Qwen3-32B\n628\t    在 instruction following 和 controlled generation 任务上经过更充分的训练。 NLI pass rate 0.81\n629\t    vs 0.88 的差距来自 Llama 在 style rewriting 时更容易引入 minor content modifications (添加 qualifiers,\n630\t    重组 argument structure)。 Pairwise win rate 衰减到 62.5% (vs Qwen 的 69.1%) 有两个可能原因：(a)\n631\t    lower NLI pass rate → 更多边缘质量的 counterfactual 被保留 (NLI 0.81-0.90 的样本 content preservation\n632\t    较差) → diluting the signal；(b) Llama 的 style transfer 不够 \"extreme\" — formal counterfactual\n633\t    不够 formal，contrast 较小。但方向完全 一致 (formal wins)，p=0.042 显著，6.6pp 差异在 Qwen 的 CI 内\n634\t    (p_diff=0.43)。 这足以 rule out \"Qwen-specific artifact\" 但引入 nuance: \"rewriter choice\n635\t    moderates effect magnitude (~7pp) even when direction is robust.\" 对方法论的 implication：CSD\n636\t    应报告 rewriter choice 并建议用多个 rewriter 取均值或报告 range。论文一段话足矣。\n637\t\n638\t    '\n639\t  tables:\n640\t  - name: 'Table S3: Rewriter robustness check'\n641\t    description: '2 rows (Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B) × columns: NLI_pass_rate, BERTScore_pass_rate,\n642\t      n_consistent, formal_win_rate (CI, p), direction_asymmetry。Footnote: chi-squared\n643\t      test for win_rate difference p=0.43。\n644\t\n645\t      '\n646\t  figures_description:\n647\t  - 'Two-bar chart with error bars: Qwen (blue) and Llama (green) formal_win_rate\n648\t    with 95% Wilson CI。Both above 50% line, CIs overlapping。Simple, clean robustness\n649\t    visualization。\n650\t\n651\t    '\n652\t  analysis: 'exp-009 是 reviewer 几乎必问的 robustness check。Median 结果提供 clean answer： \"direction\n653\t    robust, magnitude varies.\" 论文中 1-2 段：acknowledge rewriter dependence, recommend\n654\t    reporting rewriter choice as method parameter。如果 reviewer 要求第三个 rewriter，可以 argue\n655\t    \"two independent rewriters with consistent direction provides reasonable evidence\n656\t    against rewriter-specific artifacts; exhaustive rewriter comparison is beyond\n657\t    scope.\" Cost: 8 GPU hours for Llama-70B generation。\n658\t\n659\t    '\n660\t- name: Human NLI validation\n661\t  plan_id: exp-013\n662\t  description: '100 counterfactual pairs 的 human annotation (content preservation\n663\t    judgment)。 报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen''s kappa)、precision、recall。使用 LLM-as-annotator\n664\t    + human spot check。\n665\t\n666\t    '\n667\t  expected_results:\n668\t    annotation_summary:\n669\t      n_annotated: 100\n670\t      human_pass: 95\n671\t      human_fail: 5\n672\t      nli_pass: 88\n673\t      nli_fail: 12\n674\t    confusion_matrix:\n675\t      tp: 87\n676\t      fp: 1\n677\t      fn: 8\n678\t      tn: 4\n679\t    agreement_metrics:\n680\t      raw_agreement: 0.91\n681\t      cohens_kappa: 0.43\n682\t      pabak: 0.82\n683\t      prevalence_index: 0.83\n684\t    precision_recall:\n685\t      nli_precision: 0.989\n686\t      nli_recall: 0.916\n687\t      nli_f1: 0.951\n688\t      nli_specificity: 0.8\n689\t    false_negative_analysis:\n690\t      n_false_negatives: 8\n691\t      categories:\n692\t        paraphrase_level_changes: 5\n693\t        minor_lexical_substitution: 2\n694\t        borderline_content_addition: 1\n695\t      mean_nli_score_of_fn: 0.78\n696\t      note: FNs cluster at NLI 0.75-0.88 — NLI is strict on borderline cases\n697\t    false_positive_analysis:\n698\t      n_false_positives: 1\n699\t      category: subtle_factual_drift\n700\t      nli_score: 0.93\n701\t      note: NLI missed minor factual change that human caught; extremely rare\n702\t  result_rationale: 'Kappa=0.43 看似平庸但实际由 class imbalance 驱动而非真正 disagreement。 机制：100\n703\t    pairs 中 95 个 human 判 \"pass\"、5 个 \"fail\"。在 base rate 95% 的 情况下，即使完美 agreement 在\n704\t    majority class、只有少量 minority class 分歧， kappa 也会被严重压低。具体：8 个 false negative (NLI\n705\t    reject human accept)  来自 NLI 对 borderline 变化的过严判断——NLI entailment model 对 paraphrase\n706\t    级 别的词汇替换 (synonyms, sentence restructuring) 给出 0.75-0.88 分，低于 0.90 threshold，但\n707\t    human annotator 认为 content preserved。这说明 NLI gate 是 \"conservative\" 而非 \"wrong\"——它丢弃了\n708\t    human 认为 OK 的 borderline cases， 损失 recall (8/95=8.4%) 但不损失 precision (只有 1/88=1.1%\n709\t    false positive)。 对论文的影响：NLI gate 通过的 counterfactual 几乎确定 content preserved (precision\n710\t    98.9%)，这才是实验设计需要的保证。recall 损失只影响 effective n (sample size reduction ~12%)，不影响\n711\t    validity。PABAK=0.82 (excellent agreement) 在 class imbalance 校正后远高于 raw kappa。但\n712\t    reviewer 可能只看 kappa headline → 需要 proactive defense。\n713\t\n714\t    '\n715\t  tables:\n716\t  - name: 'Table S4: Human validation confusion matrix'\n717\t    description: '2×2 matrix with margins。Below: kappa=0.43, PABAK=0.82, prevalence\n718\t      index=0.83, precision=98.9%, recall=91.6%。Footnote explaining PABAK and why\n719\t      it''s more appropriate than raw kappa at 95% base rate。\n720\t\n721\t      '\n722\t  - name: 'Table S5: False negative error analysis'\n723\t    description: '8 FN examples。Columns: sample_id, NLI_score, change_type (paraphrase/\n724\t      lexical/borderline), human_judgment_confidence, example_excerpt。 Shows NLI is\n725\t      strict-but-reasonable on borderline cases。\n726\t\n727\t      '\n728\t  figures_description:\n729\t  - 'Histogram: NLI entailment score distribution, split by human judgment (pass=blue,\n730\t    fail=red)。X-axis: NLI score 0-1。Vertical dashed at 0.90 threshold。Shows clear\n731\t    separation: human-fail cases cluster at NLI<0.70, human-pass cases cluster at\n732\t    NLI>0.90, with small overlap zone 0.75-0.88 where FNs live。Demonstrates threshold\n733\t    choice is reasonable。\n734\t\n735\t    '\n736\t  analysis: exp-013 需要最 careful 的 presentation。论文策略：(1) §3.2 先 report precision 98.9%\n737\t    和 \"conservative gate\" framing（\"our NLI gate prioritizes precision over recall\n738\t    — passed pairs are near-certainly content-preserving\"）；(2) Full metrics including\n739\t    kappa 放在 §3.2 的后半段或 Appendix A，accompanied by class imbalance discussion；(3) PABAK=0.82\n740\t    作为 robustness metric；(4) 3 annotated examples in Appendix (1 TP, 1 TN, 1 FN showing\n741\t    NLI's conservative behavior)。如果 reviewer 仍 push back on kappa<0.60，rebuttal 的核心论点：\"Cohen's\n742\t    kappa is known to underestimate agreement under extreme class imbalance (Feinstein\n743\t    & Cicchetti 1990, Prevalence Index = 0.83); PABAK corrects for this (0.82, excellent\n744\t    agreement). More importantly, our experimental design requires that passed pairs\n745\t    preserve content (precision = 98.9%), not that all content-preserving pairs pass\n746\t    (recall). The 8.4% recall loss reduces effective sample size but does not compromise\n747\t    validity.\"\n748\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a33c06a6-9d6e-466c-b93b-d82fa976056a","uuid":"db3fe81c-f5d8-4308-9fba-f5b1586fd376","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:46:12.274Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T010111/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Claims require softening but paper remains viable. C1 holds but\n  generalization downgrades from \"across judges and benchmarks\" to \"demonstrated on\n  GPT-4o, replicated on Gemini-Flash, with supporting evidence on AlpacaEval.\" C2\n  remains headline but qualified: \"Likert Blindspot is robust for strong-bias conditions\n  (GPT-4o × formality on LLMBar) but gap magnitude is condition-dependent; at n=500\n  binarized Likert approaches significance → Blindspot is primarily an efficiency\n  gap (~2× Cohen''s h), not absolute insensitivity.\" C3 drops \"multi-axis\" — formality\n  is validated, verbosity is \"suggestive\" (H1 PASS but scoring blocked), tone/register\n  are method boundaries. C4 provides detection guidance only; no correction formula\n  without multi-cell backing. RATE differentiation paragraph works (RATE uses Likert\n  ATE → our C2 applies to RATE itself) but is speculative without RATE replication\n  data. Direction asymmetry varies by judge → no unified causal narrative across judges.\n  Compensate with deeper methodological analysis (why does GPT-4o × LLMBar work so\n  well?), honest boundary characterization, power analysis as practical tool, stronger\n  psychometric lineage framing. Target: EMNLP 2026 Findings (confident) / Main (borderline,\n  needs strong rebuttal on generalization). Expected ARR score: 3.0–3.5.\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: '在 Claude-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 LLMBar formality pairwise 实验。\n    使用已有 counterfactuals，200 pairwise calls × 2 directions per judge， position-controlled\n    dual-direction protocol。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    claude_sonnet:\n      n_valid_both_trials: 96\n      n_consistent: 50\n      consistency_rate: 0.521\n      formal_wins: 29\n      casual_wins: 21\n      formal_win_rate: 0.58\n      wilson_ci:\n      - 0.442\n      - 0.706\n      sign_test_p: 0.161\n      position_bias_overall_A: 0.52\n      direction_formal_to_casual:\n        n: 30\n        formal_wins: 19\n        win_rate: 0.633\n        p: 0.1\n      direction_casual_to_formal:\n        n: 20\n        formal_wins: 10\n        win_rate: 0.5\n        p: 1.0\n    gemini_20_flash:\n      n_valid_both_trials: 97\n      n_consistent: 47\n      consistency_rate: 0.485\n      formal_wins: 30\n      casual_wins: 17\n      formal_win_rate: 0.638\n      wilson_ci:\n      - 0.495\n      - 0.761\n      sign_test_p: 0.041\n      position_bias_overall_A: 0.56\n      direction_formal_to_casual:\n        n: 28\n        formal_wins: 22\n        win_rate: 0.786\n        p: 0.002\n      direction_casual_to_formal:\n        n: 19\n        formal_wins: 8\n        win_rate: 0.421\n        p: 0.648\n    cross_judge_summary:\n      judges_significant_p005: 1\n      judges_marginal_p005_015: 1\n      judges_null: 0\n      gpt4o_reference_win_rate: 0.691\n      best_non_gpt4o_win_rate: 0.638\n      win_rate_attenuation_vs_gpt4o: 0.053\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档预测 style bias 是真实效应但跨 judge 有系统性衰减。Gemini-Flash 显著 (p=0.041)\n    的机制：Flash 模型的 RLHF 投入较少 debiasing → 保留更强的 surface style preference；但效应量从 GPT-4o\n    的 69.1% 衰减到 63.8%，因为 Gemini 的 pairwise 一致性率较低 (48.5% vs GPT-4o 56.1%)，引入更多噪声对。Claude-Sonnet\n    不显著 (p=0.161) 的机制：Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程更保守，Constitutional AI 训练 可能部分抑制 surface style\n    preference；加上 Claude 的 consistency_rate 只有 52.1%，有效 n 从 50 对中仅 29 个 formal wins\n    → 检验力不足。Direction asymmetry 的 judge 间差异是 median 档的关键特征：Gemini 与 GPT-4o 类似，formal→casual\n    方向强 (78.6%)、casual→formal 方向 null (42.1%)；但 Claude 的不对称性更弱 (63.3% vs 50.0%)，且\n    casual→formal 方向完全平坦。这使得 \"formal→casual 方向 驱动效应\" 的叙事不能跨 judge 推广——只能说 \"direction\n    asymmetry is judge-dependent, consistently observed for GPT-4o and Gemini but\n    not Claude.\" 一致性率的 judge 间差异本身值得报告：它反映不同 judge 的 position sensitivity， 不是方法的失败而是\n    judge 特性的测量。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2a: Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar)'\n    description: '3 rows (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) × columns: n_consistent,\n      consistency_rate, formal_win_rate, 95% Wilson CI, sign_test_p, formal→casual_win_rate,\n      casual→formal_win_rate, position_bias. GPT-4o 行 bolded (primary)，Gemini 行 starred\n      (significant replication)。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: formal_win_rate with 95% Wilson CI for 3 judges。Vertical dashed\n    line at 50%。GPT-4o CI clearly right of 50%；Gemini CI right but wider，lower bound\n    near 50%；Claude CI straddling 50%。Annotate p-values next to each bar。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'C1 表述降级为 \"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006), replicated on Gemini-Flash\n    (p=0.041), not detected on Claude-Sonnet (p=0.161, possibly underpowered).\" Claude\n    的 null 不能确定是 \"无 bias\" 还是 \"power 不足\"——需在论文中讨论 power (at n=50 consistent, MDE≈0.18\n    for pairwise win_rate → 58% 在 detection boundary 上)。Direction asymmetry 的 judge\n    间差异增加了 §5 Discussion 的复杂度但也增加 了 depth——\"why does asymmetry vary?\" 可以链接到 judge\n    的 RLHF 训练差异。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上新生成 formality counterfactuals，GPT-4o + Claude-Sonnet\n    + Gemini-Flash 作为 judge 运行完整 CSD pairwise pipeline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    counterfactual_generation:\n      alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n      alpacaeval_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.79\n      alpacaeval_both_pass_rate: 0.78\n      mtbench_nli_pass_rate: 0.79\n      mtbench_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.74\n      mtbench_both_pass_rate: 0.72\n      note: NLI pass rate drops vs LLMBar (0.88) due to more diverse/technical source\n        texts\n    alpacaeval:\n      gpt4o:\n        n_consistent: 51\n        formal_win_rate: 0.608\n        sign_test_p: 0.072\n        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.7\n        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n      claude_sonnet:\n        n_consistent: 44\n        formal_win_rate: 0.545\n        sign_test_p: 0.348\n        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.58\n        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n      gemini_flash:\n        n_consistent: 42\n        formal_win_rate: 0.595\n        sign_test_p: 0.109\n        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.68\n        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.48\n    mt_bench:\n      gpt4o:\n        n_consistent: 46\n        formal_win_rate: 0.565\n        sign_test_p: 0.214\n        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.62\n        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n      claude_sonnet:\n        n_consistent: 40\n        formal_win_rate: 0.525\n        sign_test_p: 0.557\n        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.54\n        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n      gemini_flash:\n        n_consistent: 39\n        formal_win_rate: 0.538\n        sign_test_p: 0.396\n        direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.6\n        direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.47\n    cross_benchmark_summary:\n      cells_significant_p005: 0\n      cells_trend_p005_010: 1\n      cells_trend_p010_015: 1\n      cells_null: 4\n      benchmark_ordering: LLMBar >> AlpacaEval > MT-Bench\n      nli_pass_rate_ordering: LLMBar (0.88) > AlpacaEval (0.83) > MT-Bench (0.79)\n  result_rationale: '新 benchmark 效应衰减是 median 档的核心预测。两个独立机制叠加造成衰减： (1) Counterfactual\n    质量下降——LLMBar 源文本是简洁的 instruction-following 对， formality rewriting 容易保内容；AlpacaEval\n    文本更长更多样，NLI pass rate 从 0.88 降到 0.83，丢弃更多样本 → 有效 n 减少；MT-Bench 包含数学/代码/推理等 domain\n    特异性强的文本，formality rewriting 更容易改变内容（把 \"Let''s solve this step by step\" 改成正式版本可能改变推理链结构）→\n    NLI 降到 0.79。 (2) Formality 方差差异——LLMBar 的 instruction-following 文本天然有较大的 formality\n    方差（有的回答很 casual，有的很 formal），counterfactual contrast 大； MT-Bench 的技术性文本天然偏 formal，formality\n    rewriting 的 contrast 小 → smaller effect size。GPT-4o × AlpacaEval 的 p=0.072 (trend)\n    符合 median 核心 假设 \"1 additional benchmark shows trend (p<0.10) but not clean significance\"。\n    Holm-Bonferroni 校正 (within GPT-4o: 0.006, 0.072, 0.214 → adjusted 0.018, 0.144,\n    0.214) 后只有 LLMBar survive。论文需诚实报告：\"effect replicates as trend on AlpacaEval but\n    not MT-Bench\" 并讨论 benchmark 依赖性原因。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2b: Full 3×3 judge × benchmark pairwise results'\n    description: '9-cell grid。Rows: LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench。Columns grouped by\n      judge， each showing formal_win_rate (p-value)。p<0.05 bolded，p<0.10 italicized。\n      Only 2 bold cells (GPT-4o×LLMBar, Gemini×LLMBar)，2 italic (GPT-4o×AlpacaEval,\n      Gemini×AlpacaEval)。Additional column: NLI pass rate per benchmark。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: 3×3 grid，color = formal_win_rate (diverging colormap centered at 50%)。\n    Cell annotations: win_rate% (p=x.xx)。Clear gradient: LLMBar row warmest， MT-Bench\n    row coolest。Column gradient: GPT-4o warmest，Claude coolest。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'exp-002 确认 formality bias 不是 LLMBar artifact——AlpacaEval 上 GPT-4o 和 Gemini\n    都显示 trend (p<0.12)——但 effect magnitude 确实 benchmark-dependent。 论文需要 §5.1 \"Benchmark\n    Dependence\" 讨论三个 benchmark 的差异，linking to counterfactual quality (NLI pass rate)\n    和 formality 方差。MT-Bench 的 null 结果 本身有 method boundary 意义：when source texts are\n    domain-specific/technical， formality rewriting 更可能失败 NLI gate → CSD 方法自动 degrades\n    gracefully。 Claim 从 \"across benchmarks\" 降级为 \"demonstrated on LLMBar, supporting\n    trend on AlpacaEval (instruction-following), inconclusive on MT-Bench (task-specific).\"\n\n    '\n- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: '对 9 个 judge × benchmark cells 系统计算 Likert ATE 和 binarized Likert sign\n    test，与 pairwise win rate 对比。量化 C2 Likert Blindspot 的 replication rate 和 condition-dependence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    likert_ate:\n      gpt4o_llmbar:\n        ate: -0.102\n        se: 0.149\n        p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval:\n        ate: -0.07\n        se: 0.155\n        p: 0.48\n      gpt4o_mtbench:\n        ate: -0.04\n        se: 0.161\n        p: 0.69\n      claude_llmbar:\n        ate: 0.03\n        se: 0.158\n        p: 0.71\n      claude_alpacaeval:\n        ate: -0.01\n        se: 0.165\n        p: 0.88\n      claude_mtbench:\n        ate: 0.02\n        se: 0.17\n        p: 0.82\n      gemini_llmbar:\n        ate: -0.09\n        se: 0.152\n        p: 0.39\n      gemini_alpacaeval:\n        ate: -0.06\n        se: 0.16\n        p: 0.53\n      gemini_mtbench:\n        ate: -0.03\n        se: 0.168\n        p: 0.76\n      any_significant: false\n      note: Likert ATE non-significant in all 9 cells; continuous Likert uniformly\n        insensitive\n    binarized_likert:\n      gpt4o_llmbar:\n        n_nontie: 33\n        win_rate: 0.606\n        p: 0.296\n        status: non-significant\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval:\n        n_nontie: 29\n        win_rate: 0.586\n        p: 0.108\n        status: ambiguous\n      gpt4o_mtbench:\n        n_nontie: 26\n        win_rate: 0.538\n        p: 0.422\n        status: non-significant\n      claude_llmbar:\n        n_nontie: 27\n        win_rate: 0.556\n        p: 0.248\n        status: non-significant\n      claude_alpacaeval:\n        n_nontie: 23\n        win_rate: 0.522\n        p: 0.621\n        status: non-significant\n      claude_mtbench:\n        n_nontie: 21\n        win_rate: 0.524\n        p: 0.617\n        status: non-significant\n      gemini_llmbar:\n        n_nontie: 30\n        win_rate: 0.6\n        p: 0.098\n        status: ambiguous\n      gemini_alpacaeval:\n        n_nontie: 25\n        win_rate: 0.56\n        p: 0.23\n        status: non-significant\n      gemini_mtbench:\n        n_nontie: 22\n        win_rate: 0.5\n        p: 1.0\n        status: non-significant\n    binarized_likert_summary:\n      non_significant_cells: 7\n      ambiguous_cells_p005_012: 2\n      significant_cells: 0\n    c2_gap_analysis:\n      cells_pairwise_sig_AND_likert_not: 2\n      cells_pairwise_sig_AND_binarized_ambiguous: 1\n      cells_pairwise_trend_AND_binarized_ambiguous: 1\n      cells_both_non_sig: 5\n      c2_clean_replication_rate: 0.67\n      c2_with_ambiguous: 0.5\n    measurement_amplification:\n      mean_pairwise_effect_over_50pct: 0.074\n      mean_binarized_likert_effect_over_50pct: 0.044\n      amplification_ratio: 1.68\n  result_rationale: 'Likert ATE 全面不显著是 median 档的稳健预测——continuous Likert 的 within-pair\n    评分方差 (SE~0.15-0.17) 远大于 formality ATE (~0.05-0.10)，信噪比根本不足。 这是 structural 而非 power\n    issue：即使 n→∞，如果 ATE 接近零（raw ATE 在 -0.10 到 +0.03 之间散布），continuous Likert 的 measurement\n    noise 使得 effect 不 convergent。Binarized Likert 的 2 个 ambiguous cells 是 C2 的最大叙事张力：\n    (a) Gemini×LLMBar binarized p=0.098 vs pairwise p=0.041——gap 存在但不大， reviewer 会质疑\n    \"is this just a power issue?\" 回答：effect size 差异（63.8% vs 60.0%）说明 pairwise 不仅\n    more powerful 而且 amplifies the signal—— amplification ratio 1.68× 是 structural\n    advantage（pairwise 的 forced choice 消除了 Likert 的 tie/neutral responses 噪声）。(b)\n    GPT-4o×AlpacaEval binarized p=0.108 vs pairwise p=0.072——两个都 marginal，gap 极小 →\n    这个 cell 不支持 C2。但在 5 个 null cells 中，pairwise 和 binarized Likert 都 null → C2 gap\n    只在 effect 存在时才有意义。整体：C2 replication rate 67%（2/3 significant pairwise cells 有\n    clean gap），但加入 ambiguous 考量降到 50%。论文需要 nuanced 表述：\"The Likert Blindspot is most\n    pronounced when style bias is moderate (pairwise 60-70%); for strong effects,\n    binarized Likert may approach detection; for null effects, no method detects.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Main results — Pairwise vs Likert vs Binarized Likert (9 cells)'\n    description: 'Paper 的 main result table。9-cell grid (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)，\n      each cell: Pairwise win_rate (p) | Likert ATE (p) | Binarized win_rate (p)。\n      Color coding: green p<0.05, yellow p<0.12, red p>0.12。 Final row: measurement\n      amplification ratio per cell。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table S1: C2 gap categorization'\n    description: 'Supplementary。Rows: 9 cells。Columns: pairwise_status (sig/marginal/null),\n      binarized_status (non-sig/ambiguous), C2_gap (clean/ambiguous/no gap/NA)。 Summary:\n      2 clean, 1 ambiguous, 1 marginal-both, 5 both-null。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired lollipop chart: 9 cells on y-axis，for each cell two dots connected by\n    line — pairwise win_rate (blue) and binarized Likert win_rate (orange)。 Vertical\n    dashed at 50%。Gap between dots = C2 blindspot magnitude per cell。 Cells ordered\n    by pairwise effect size。Clearly shows pairwise dots consistently further from\n    50% than binarized Likert dots。\n\n    '\n  - 'Scatter: x = pairwise win_rate, y = binarized Likert win_rate, one point per\n    cell。 y=x diagonal line。All points below diagonal → pairwise always ≥ binarized。\n    Regression line slope < 1 → amplification ratio quantified。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'exp-003 是论文最重要的表格。Median 结果的叙事策略：(1) Lead with Likert ATE = 0/9 significant\n    → continuous Likert 完全 blind，这是最强 version of C2；(2) Binarized Likert = 0/9 significant\n    (2 ambiguous) vs Pairwise = 2/9 significant → gap exists but C2 需要 qualify 为 \"Likert\n    Blindspot is a measurement efficiency gap, not absolute insensitivity\"；(3) Amplification\n    ratio 1.68× provides quantitative hook for practitioners。§5.2 \"When Does the Blindspot\n    Narrow?\" 分析 C2 gap 与 effect size 的关系——如果 pairwise effect 越大 gap 越大 (positive correlation)，说明\n    Likert 对所有 effect size 都 equally insensitive (stronger C2)；如果 gap 恒定， 说明只是 constant\n    offset (weaker C2 but still useful)。\n\n    '\n- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: '对所有 judge × benchmark 组合做 original vs double-rewrite pairwise comparison，\n    量化 original preference confound。扩展 exp-014 的 GEE logistic decomposition 到所有条件。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    original_preference_pairwise:\n      gpt4o_llmbar:\n        original_pref_win_rate: 0.585\n        original_pref_p: 0.052\n        gee_original_OR: 1.82\n        gee_original_p: 0.052\n        note: known from exp-014\n      claude_llmbar:\n        original_pref_win_rate: 0.545\n        original_pref_p: 0.232\n        gee_original_OR: 1.38\n        gee_original_p: 0.245\n      gemini_llmbar:\n        original_pref_win_rate: 0.625\n        original_pref_p: 0.026\n        gee_original_OR: 2.18\n        gee_original_p: 0.03\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval:\n        original_pref_win_rate: 0.57\n        original_pref_p: 0.105\n        gee_original_OR: 1.58\n        gee_original_p: 0.112\n      claude_alpacaeval:\n        original_pref_win_rate: 0.53\n        original_pref_p: 0.396\n        gee_original_OR: 1.22\n        gee_original_p: 0.41\n      gemini_alpacaeval:\n        original_pref_win_rate: 0.58\n        original_pref_p: 0.075\n        gee_original_OR: 1.72\n        gee_original_p: 0.082\n    logistic_decomposition_extended:\n      gpt4o_llmbar:\n        formality_OR: 2.21\n        formality_p: 0.01\n        original_OR: 1.82\n        original_p: 0.052\n        formality_exceeds_original: true\n      gemini_llmbar:\n        formality_OR: 1.95\n        formality_p: 0.038\n        original_OR: 2.18\n        original_p: 0.03\n        formality_exceeds_original: false\n        note: 'CRITICAL: original preference OR exceeds formality OR for Gemini'\n      claude_llmbar:\n        formality_OR: 1.52\n        formality_p: 0.165\n        original_OR: 1.38\n        original_p: 0.245\n        formality_exceeds_original: true\n        note: neither significant — underpowered\n    summary:\n      judges_with_significant_original_pref: 1\n      judges_with_marginal_original_pref: 2\n      formality_still_dominates_for_gpt4o: true\n      confound_problematic_for_gemini: true\n  result_rationale: 'Original preference confound 在 median 档变得 judge-dependent，核心威胁来自\n    Gemini。机制：double-rewrite 虽设计为 style-preserving，仍不可避免引入 surface 变化（lexical micro-substitutions,\n    sentence structure 微调）。不同 judge 对 这些 \"rewriting artifacts\" 的敏感度不同。Gemini-Flash\n    作为较小模型，对 surface form 变化更敏感 → double-rewrite 产生的微小质量损失被 Gemini 放大为显著 original\n    preference (OR=2.18, p=0.026)。关键问题：Gemini×LLMBar 的 formality pairwise 显著 (p=0.041)，但\n    original preference 也显著 (p=0.026)，且 original OR (2.18) > formality OR (1.95) →\n    对 Gemini 来说，无法 cleanly separate formality bias from rewriting artifact。GPT-4o×LLMBar\n    保持 clean：formality OR (2.21) > original OR (1.82)，formality p=0.010 vs original\n    p=0.052 → 可以 argue formality is the dominant effect。Claude 两者都不显著，无信息量。论文策略： primary\n    claim 基于 GPT-4o×LLMBar (clean decomposition)；Gemini 的显著结果作为 \"replication with\n    caveat\" — \"formality bias detected (p=0.041) but original preference cannot be\n    ruled out as partial contributor (p=0.026).\" 这种 honesty 是 strength not weakness\n    — reviewer 更信任 acknowledged confounds。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: Original preference decomposition across judges'\n    description: 'Rows: judge × benchmark (6 cells with data)。Columns: formality_OR\n      (CI, p), original_pref_OR (CI, p), formality > original?, status。 GPT-4o×LLMBar\n      highlighted as clean decomposition；Gemini×LLMBar flagged。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired forest plot: for each cell，two horizontal bars with 95% CI — formality\n    OR (blue) and original preference OR (red)。Vertical line at OR=1。 GPT-4o×LLMBar:\n    blue clearly right, red CI crossing 1。 Gemini×LLMBar: both right of 1 with overlapping\n    CIs → confound visible。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'exp-005 使得 \"confound is negligible\" argument 不成立。但 \"confound is acknowledged\n    and statistically controlled\" 在 GPT-4o 上仍然成立。对于 Gemini， 论文需要 paragraph: \"Gemini-Flash\n    shows both formality preference and original preference; future work with larger\n    n or improved double-rewrite protocol may achieve cleaner separation.\" 这实际上提供了有用的\n    method boundary：CSD 的 confound control 对某些 judge 更 effective（GPT-4o）比其他（Gemini）。\n    Practical implication for C4：recommend running original-preference control for\n    each judge, and only report formality estimates where decomposition is clean。\n\n    '\n- name: Scaled replication (n=500)\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'GPT-4o × LLMBar (最佳 cell) 从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。计算 pairwise、 binarized\n    Likert、Likert ATE，直接检验 C2 是 structural blindspot 还是 power issue。Power analysis\n    量化 measurement efficiency gap。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pairwise:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 490\n      n_consistent: 275\n      consistency_rate: 0.561\n      formal_wins: 168\n      casual_wins: 107\n      formal_win_rate: 0.611\n      wilson_ci:\n      - 0.552\n      - 0.667\n      sign_test_p: 0.0004\n    binarized_likert:\n      n_nli_ge90: 435\n      n_nontie: 163\n      formal_direction: 94\n      formal_win_rate: 0.577\n      sign_test_p: 0.063\n      wilson_ci:\n      - 0.499\n      - 0.651\n      note: Approaches significance; NOT significant at alpha=0.05\n    likert_ate:\n      n_primary: 435\n      raw_ate: -0.085\n      raw_se: 0.065\n      raw_p: 0.19\n      corrected_ate: 0.095\n      corrected_se: 0.047\n      corrected_p: 0.043\n      note: Raw ATE still wrong direction; corrected ATE barely significant\n    power_analysis:\n      pairwise_detected_effect_cohens_h: 0.222\n      binarized_likert_detected_effect_cohens_h: 0.154\n      measurement_amplification_ratio: 1.44\n      pairwise_power_at_n100: 0.72\n      pairwise_power_at_n200: 0.93\n      pairwise_power_at_n500: 0.998\n      binarized_likert_power_at_n100: 0.18\n      binarized_likert_power_at_n200: 0.34\n      binarized_likert_power_at_n500: 0.52\n      binarized_likert_n_for_80pct_power: 680\n      likert_ate_power_at_n100: 0.09\n      likert_ate_power_at_n500: 0.31\n      likert_ate_n_for_80pct_power: 1200\n    regression_to_mean:\n      n100_pairwise_win_rate: 0.691\n      n500_pairwise_win_rate: 0.611\n      regression_magnitude: 0.08\n      note: 8pp regression consistent with sampling variance at n=55 consistent pairs\n  result_rationale: 'n=500 的三个关键结果及其 rationale： (1) Pairwise win rate 从 69.1% 回归到\n    61.1%。n=100 的 69.1% 来自仅 55 个 consistent pairs → 采样方差大，Wilson CI [56.0%, 79.7%]。n=500\n    的 275 个 consistent pairs 给出更精确的 true effect estimate ~61%。8pp 回归幅度在 n=55 的 CI\n    范围内，统计上完全预期。效应仍高度显著 (p=0.0004)。 (2) Binarized Likert p=0.063：在 n=500 下 approaching\n    但 NOT crossing 0.05 线。 这是 median 档的精妙预测——如果 binarized Likert 真的 significant，C2\n    从 \"blindspot\" 变成 \"efficiency gap\"，论文核心受损；如果完全 null，C2 过于强势 反而可疑。p=0.063 恰好在模糊地带：它说明\n    binarized Likert 不是完全 blind（有 trending signal），但需要远超 pairwise 的样本量才能 detect →\n    \"efficiency gap\" framing 是准确的。关键：binarized Likert n_nontie=163 (Likert 评分相同的 pair\n    被丢弃 → 信息损失)，effective n 仅 pairwise 的 59%，这是 structural 不是 power。 (3) Likert ATE\n    raw p=0.19 仍不显著且方向错误 → continuous Likert 在 n=500 下 仍然 blind。Corrected ATE (accounting\n    for rewrite bias) p=0.043 barely significant，但 \"corrected\" 需要知道 rewrite bias →\n    不是 post-hoc 可用的检测 工具。这进一步支持 \"Likert cannot serve as style bias detector without\n    correction.\" Power analysis 的实用价值：pairwise 在 n=100 就有 72% power (接近 80%)， binarized\n    Likert 需要 n=680 for 80% power → 6.8× 样本量差距。这是论文的 quantitative C2 claim：\"pairwise\n    comparison is ~7× more sample-efficient than binarized Likert for detecting style\n    bias at the observed effect size.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Scaled replication — measurement comparison at n=500'\n    description: '3 rows (Pairwise, Binarized Likert, Likert ATE) × columns: n_effective,\n      effect_estimate, 95% CI, p-value, Cohen''s h, power_at_n100, power_at_n500,\n      n_for_80pct_power。Clearly shows efficiency hierarchy。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table S2: n=100 vs n=500 comparison'\n    description: 'Side-by-side: all metrics at two sample sizes。Regression to mean\n      quantified and contextualized。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Power curve: x = total sample size (50 to 1000), y = statistical power (0 to\n    1)。 Three curves: pairwise (blue, crosses 80% at ~110), binarized Likert (orange,\n    crosses 80% at ~680), Likert ATE (red, crosses 80% at ~1200)。Horizontal dashed\n    at 80%。Vertical dashed at n=100 and n=500。This is C2''s key visualization — the\n    efficiency gap is immediately visible。\n\n    '\n  - 'Running estimate plot: x = cumulative n (in increments of 50), y = pairwise win_rate\n    with running 95% CI ribbon。Shows convergence from volatile ~69% at n=100 toward\n    stable ~61% at n=500。Communicates regression to mean visually。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'exp-006 redefines C2 from \"Likert Blindspot\" to \"Likert Efficiency Gap.\"\n    Binarized Likert p=0.063 at n=500 means the effect is detectable in principle\n    — given enough data. But the practical gap (pairwise needs n~110, binarized Likert\n    needs n~680) is the real contribution. For practitioners: \"If you suspect style\n    bias, pairwise comparison with n=100 is sufficient; Likert scoring would need\n    n≥700 for the same statistical power.\" Title 可能需要从 \"Blindspot\" 软化为 \"Blind Spot\"\n    或保留但 在 abstract 中 qualify。Power analysis table 是最 reviewer-friendly 的结果之一—— 直接\n    actionable guidance。Win rate 回归到 61.1% 需要 honestly report，不要 buried in supplement。\n\n    '\n- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上 重复 formality\n    counterfactual generation + pairwise pipeline。排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    counterfactual_quality:\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.75\n      both_pass_rate: 0.73\n      nli_mean: 0.869\n      bertscore_mean: 0.905\n      nli_std: 0.298\n      comparison_vs_qwen:\n        qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n        qwen_both_pass_rate: 0.88\n        llama_nli_delta: -0.07\n        note: Llama slightly worse at style transfer precision\n    pairwise_results:\n      n_valid_both_trials: 95\n      n_consistent: 48\n      consistency_rate: 0.505\n      formal_wins: 30\n      casual_wins: 18\n      formal_win_rate: 0.625\n      wilson_ci:\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.749\n      sign_test_p: 0.042\n      direction_f2c_win_rate: 0.72\n      direction_c2f_win_rate: 0.5\n    comparison_with_qwen:\n      qwen_win_rate: 0.691\n      llama_win_rate: 0.625\n      difference: 0.066\n      difference_p: 0.43\n      direction_consistent: true\n      sign_consistent: true\n      magnitude_within_qwen_ci: true\n      note: 6.6pp difference not significant; both within Qwen's [56.0%, 79.7%] CI\n  result_rationale: 'Llama-3.1-70B 的 style transfer 质量略低于 Qwen3-32B 是预期中的——Qwen3-32B\n    在 instruction following 和 controlled generation 任务上经过更充分的训练。 NLI pass rate 0.81\n    vs 0.88 的差距来自 Llama 在 style rewriting 时更容易引入 minor content modifications (添加 qualifiers,\n    重组 argument structure)。 Pairwise win rate 衰减到 62.5% (vs Qwen 的 69.1%) 有两个可能原因：(a)\n    lower NLI pass rate → 更多边缘质量的 counterfactual 被保留 (NLI 0.81-0.90 的样本 content preservation\n    较差) → diluting the signal；(b) Llama 的 style transfer 不够 \"extreme\" — formal counterfactual\n    不够 formal，contrast 较小。但方向完全 一致 (formal wins)，p=0.042 显著，6.6pp 差异在 Qwen 的 CI 内\n    (p_diff=0.43)。 这足以 rule out \"Qwen-specific artifact\" 但引入 nuance: \"rewriter choice\n    moderates effect magnitude (~7pp) even when direction is robust.\" 对方法论的 implication：CSD\n    应报告 rewriter choice 并建议用多个 rewriter 取均值或报告 range。论文一段话足矣。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S3: Rewriter robustness check'\n    description: '2 rows (Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B) × columns: NLI_pass_rate, BERTScore_pass_rate,\n      n_consistent, formal_win_rate (CI, p), direction_asymmetry。Footnote: chi-squared\n      test for win_rate difference p=0.43。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Two-bar chart with error bars: Qwen (blue) and Llama (green) formal_win_rate\n    with 95% Wilson CI。Both above 50% line, CIs overlapping。Simple, clean robustness\n    visualization。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'exp-009 是 reviewer 几乎必问的 robustness check。Median 结果提供 clean answer： \"direction\n    robust, magnitude varies.\" 论文中 1-2 段：acknowledge rewriter dependence, recommend\n    reporting rewriter choice as method parameter。如果 reviewer 要求第三个 rewriter，可以 argue\n    \"two independent rewriters with consistent direction provides reasonable evidence\n    against rewriter-specific artifacts; exhaustive rewriter comparison is beyond\n    scope.\" Cost: 8 GPU hours for Llama-70B generation。\n\n    '\n- name: Human NLI validation\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: '100 counterfactual pairs 的 human annotation (content preservation\n    judgment)。 报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen''s kappa)、precision、recall。使用 LLM-as-annotator\n    + human spot check。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    annotation_summary:\n      n_annotated: 100\n      human_pass: 95\n      human_fail: 5\n      nli_pass: 88\n      nli_fail: 12\n    confusion_matrix:\n      tp: 87\n      fp: 1\n      fn: 8\n      tn: 4\n    agreement_metrics:\n      raw_agreement: 0.91\n      cohens_kappa: 0.43\n      pabak: 0.82\n      prevalence_index: 0.83\n    precision_recall:\n      nli_precision: 0.989\n      nli_recall: 0.916\n      nli_f1: 0.951\n      nli_specificity: 0.8\n    false_negative_analysis:\n      n_false_negatives: 8\n      categories:\n        paraphrase_level_changes: 5\n        minor_lexical_substitution: 2\n        borderline_content_addition: 1\n      mean_nli_score_of_fn: 0.78\n      note: FNs cluster at NLI 0.75-0.88 — NLI is strict on borderline cases\n    false_positive_analysis:\n      n_false_positives: 1\n      category: subtle_factual_drift\n      nli_score: 0.93\n      note: NLI missed minor factual change that human caught; extremely rare\n  result_rationale: 'Kappa=0.43 看似平庸但实际由 class imbalance 驱动而非真正 disagreement。 机制：100\n    pairs 中 95 个 human 判 \"pass\"、5 个 \"fail\"。在 base rate 95% 的 情况下，即使完美 agreement 在\n    majority class、只有少量 minority class 分歧， kappa 也会被严重压低。具体：8 个 false negative (NLI\n    reject human accept)  来自 NLI 对 borderline 变化的过严判断——NLI entailment model 对 paraphrase\n    级 别的词汇替换 (synonyms, sentence restructuring) 给出 0.75-0.88 分，低于 0.90 threshold，但\n    human annotator 认为 content preserved。这说明 NLI gate 是 \"conservative\" 而非 \"wrong\"——它丢弃了\n    human 认为 OK 的 borderline cases， 损失 recall (8/95=8.4%) 但不损失 precision (只有 1/88=1.1%\n    false positive)。 对论文的影响：NLI gate 通过的 counterfactual 几乎确定 content preserved (precision\n    98.9%)，这才是实验设计需要的保证。recall 损失只影响 effective n (sample size reduction ~12%)，不影响\n    validity。PABAK=0.82 (excellent agreement) 在 class imbalance 校正后远高于 raw kappa。但\n    reviewer 可能只看 kappa headline → 需要 proactive defense。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S4: Human validation confusion matrix'\n    description: '2×2 matrix with margins。Below: kappa=0.43, PABAK=0.82, prevalence\n      index=0.83, precision=98.9%, recall=91.6%。Footnote explaining PABAK and why\n      it''s more appropriate than raw kappa at 95% base rate。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table S5: False negative error analysis'\n    description: '8 FN examples。Columns: sample_id, NLI_score, change_type (paraphrase/\n      lexical/borderline), human_judgment_confidence, example_excerpt。 Shows NLI is\n      strict-but-reasonable on borderline cases。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Histogram: NLI entailment score distribution, split by human judgment (pass=blue,\n    fail=red)。X-axis: NLI score 0-1。Vertical dashed at 0.90 threshold。Shows clear\n    separation: human-fail cases cluster at NLI<0.70, human-pass cases cluster at\n    NLI>0.90, with small overlap zone 0.75-0.88 where FNs live。Demonstrates threshold\n    choice is reasonable。\n\n    '\n  analysis: exp-013 需要最 careful 的 presentation。论文策略：(1) §3.2 先 report precision 98.9%\n    和 \"conservative gate\" framing（\"our NLI gate prioritizes precision over recall\n    — passed pairs are near-certainly content-preserving\"）；(2) Full metrics including\n    kappa 放在 §3.2 的后半段或 Appendix A，accompanied by class imbalance discussion；(3) PABAK=0.82\n    作为 robustness metric；(4) 3 annotated examples in Appendix (1 TP, 1 TN, 1 FN showing\n    NLI's conservative behavior)。如果 reviewer 仍 push back on kappa<0.60，rebuttal 的核心论点：\"Cohen's\n    kappa is known to underestimate agreement under extreme class imbalance (Feinstein\n    & Cicchetti 1990, Prevalence Index = 0.83); PABAK corrects for this (0.82, excellent\n    agreement). More importantly, our experimental design requires that passed pairs\n    preserve content (precision = 98.9%), not that all content-preserving pairs pass\n    (recall). The 8.4% recall loss reduces effective sample size but does not compromise\n    validity.\"\n","numLines":748,"startLine":1,"totalLines":748}}}
